---
// src/pages/admin/help/settings.astro
// In-app reference: business hours, contact info, social links, navigation.
import AdminLayout from "@/layouts/AdminLayout.astro";
import AccentCard from "@/components/admin/AccentCard.astro";
import AccentCardHeader from "@/components/admin/AccentCardHeader.astro";
---

<AdminLayout
  title="Shop Settings"
  description="Reference for Hours, Contact, Social, and Navigation."
>
  <p class="text-(--content-body) mb-6 max-w-2xl">
    Hours, contact info, social links, and which navigation pages are
    visible. Everything here goes live the moment you save — no rebuild, no
    waiting.
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <AccentCard tone="neutral">
      <AccentCardHeader title="Settings → Hours" />
      <div class="px-4 py-4 text-sm text-(--content-body) space-y-1">
        <p>Your regular weekly schedule — this is what the open/closed badge and hours table follow automatically every day, unless overridden.</p>
        <p class="text-(--content-meta)">For a single closed day (holiday, staff event), use Notifications → Shop Status instead.</p>
      </div>
    </AccentCard>

    <AccentCard tone="neutral">
      <AccentCardHeader title="Settings → Contact" />
      <div class="px-4 py-4 text-sm text-(--content-body)">
        <p>Business name, address, phone, and email — shown in the site footer. All fields are required.</p>
      </div>
    </AccentCard>

    <AccentCard tone="neutral">
      <AccentCardHeader title="Settings → Social" />
      <div class="px-4 py-4 text-sm text-(--content-body) space-y-1">
        <p>Each active profile has its own Save and Remove button — no confirmation on Remove, so double-check before removing.</p>
        <p>Add a new profile from the dropdown — platforms already added are grayed out, since you edit an existing one instead of adding it twice.</p>
      </div>
    </AccentCard>

    <AccentCard tone="warning">
      <AccentCardHeader title="Settings → Navigation" />
      <div class="px-4 py-4 text-sm text-(--content-body) space-y-2">
        <p>Two on/off switches: <strong class="text-(--content-heading)">Sale Page</strong> and <strong class="text-(--content-heading)">The Shop Page</strong> visibility in the site nav.</p>
        <p class="text-(--content-meta)">Hiding a page doesn't delete anything — it just removes the nav link. The page and its content are untouched, and you can turn it back on any time.</p>
      </div>
    </AccentCard>
  </div>
</AdminLayout>
